==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|exact|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪɡˈzæk(t).li/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-exactly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# Of a [[manner]], without [[approximation]]; [[precisely]].
#: {{ux|en|Measure '''exactly''' so we can be sure it is right.}}
#: {{ux|en|The edge is not '''exactly''' straight.}}
#: {{ux|en|He divided the coins '''exactly''' in half.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Engliſh Teacher|first=Chriſtopher|last=Cooper|chapter=Chap. XIX: Of Barbarous Speaking|page=77-78|publisher2=Scolar Press|location2=Menston|publisher=''John Richardſon'', for the Author|location=London|year2=1969|year=1687|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/englishteacher1600coop/page/77/mode/1up|passage=He, that would write '''exactly''', muſt avoid a Barbarous Pronunciation, and conſider for facility, or thorow miſtake, many words are not ſounded after the beſt dialect. Such as {{...}} ''Wun'', one.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1976|album=w:Songs in the Key of Life|author=w:Stevie Wonder|title=w:[[As (song)|As]]|text=Just as time knew to move on since the beginning / And the seasons know '''exactly''' when to change / Just as kindness knows no shame / Know through all your joy and pain / That I'll be loving you always}}
# Of a [[focus]], [[precisely]], {{n-g|used to provide emphasis.}}
#: {{ux|en|He did it that way '''exactly''' to prove the point.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Amlynn Smith|title=Lost and Found|page=18|passage=His hair is a semilong dull red and pulled back in a sloppy pony at the base of his neck, and his face is riddled with small freckles and grease, but out here I can see personal hygiene isn't '''exactly''' at the top of the priority list.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|without approximation}} {{l|en|accurately}}, {{l|en|exact}}, {{l|en|perfectly}}; see also [[Thesaurus:exactly]]

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|without approximation}} {{l|en|approximately}}

